# `build.py` imports `navgraph.py` by name, so running the tool from the
# project root leaves a __pycache__ beside them. The repo's root .gitignore
# scopes its __pycache__ rules per test suite rather than globally; this is the
# same idea for one tool directory, and is narrower than a repo-wide rule would
# be — nothing else in `src/` is Python.
__pycache__/